'''Advanced Placement''' ('''AP''') '''Physics 2''' is a year-long introductory [[physics]] course administered by the [[College Board]] as part of its [[Advanced Placement]] program. It is intended to proxy a second-semester algebra-based university course in [[thermodynamics]], [[electromagnetism]], [[optics]], and [[modern physics]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://jacobsphysics.blogspot.com/2011/07/ap-physics-1-and-2-redesign-as-it.html|title=Jacobs Physics: AP Physics 1 and 2 Redesign (as it stands now) and Honors Physics I|first=Greg|last=Jacobs|date=25 July 2011|accessdate=4 September 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230416113849/https://jacobsphysics.blogspot.com/2011/07/ap-physics-1-and-2-redesign-as-it.html|archive-date=16 April 2023|url-status=dead}}</ref>{{self-published inline|date=March 2025}} Along with [[AP Physics 1]], the first AP Physics 2 exam was administered in 2015.

